    {
      "test_id": "ut_proof_conclusion_019",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Tier justification",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": " The stated reason does not hold. The Limits of the Conclusion section names four things needed to reach proved: a formal exhaustiveness declaration, a Preston birth and baptism register search, a nonconformist christening register search, and direct inspection of the physical register at the Lancashire Record Office. Each is framed as a gap not yet closed, which is the opposite of presenting the search as complete. The rubric pass bar asks that a probable narrative name what would be needed for proved, and it does. Raising to 3. A 2 could only stand on different grounds, that the narrative never explains why the evidence is more than possible."
